WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:52.060
Wow, that’s cold!

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.690
Perhaps the anxiety of the entrance exams made me feel…

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:59.640
this year’s summer was colder than any other.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:05.470
The semester will be over soon. We have just two months left.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.020
Nozomu-kun!

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.400
Good morning, Nozomu-kun, Kosaka-kun.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.850
Good morning.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.340
Good morning!

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.460
Take a look, Nozomu-kun.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.030
We made these.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.990
Thanks.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.890
Again, huh? Lucky you.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.770
Perhaps it’s getting too heavy?

00:02:28.770 --> 00:02:30.250
Did we make too many?

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:33.870
Oh no, nothing like that.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.060
I’m very happy.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:35.840
That’s good.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.040
Yura-chan, we have to hurry.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.720
It appears so, Kira-chan.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.300
Today’s our turn to do the duties.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.180
We have to do things like move the globe around.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:46.770
Ah, okay.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:49.050
We’ll be going ahead of you, then.

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.320
See you girls later!

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.670
It seems strange, no matter how you look at it…

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:59.620
Why are you always treated so kindly by the Sakurazuki sisters?

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.380
Why do you assume I know the answer to that…

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:07.370
Perhaps you secretly gave the Sakurazuki sisters a present or something?

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:07.920
Huh?

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.290
Those two feel bad about receiving presents, so they’re diligently paying you back.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.970
That has to be it!

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.020
That’s just wrong.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.760
If that isn’t the case, then there’s no other explanation.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:23.650
Maybe I should switch my attention to the Ichijou sisters.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.970
Nozomu-chan!

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.230
Good morning, Nozomu-chan.

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:28.830
Good morning.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:29.880
Good morning!

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.390
Good morning, Kosaka-kun.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:32.810
Good morning.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:38.740
Ah, your hair is all messed up!

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.960
Your hair has always been bouncing around like that since then.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.010
Please stop that.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:44.370
What? What are you talking about?

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:48.870
Remember back in kindergarten? Nozomu-
chan always had his hair messed up like this.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.040
I was with you guys, and I don’t recall that.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.950
For some reason, it was only that part that bounced around.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.260
I asked you to stop earlier. That’s ancient history.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.290
It’s not that far back at all.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.510
We’re talking about now.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.720
Damn, if I had that messed up hair too…

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:10.100
Oh, we heard that you’re taking the exams for Futa High.

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.130
Ah, yes.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.520
That’s good. Then we can go to the same high school.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:17.270
I’m struggling to make it by the skin of my teeth. If I don’t study hard…

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:19.650
It’ll be fine since we’re talking about you, Nozomu-chan.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.410
We’re moving on to English studies so we’ll help you with that.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.460
Oh, thanks. That’ll help me out a lot.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:28.660
Oh, did you hear? I’m trying for Wakaba High.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.540
Ah, is that so.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:34.670
It’s close to Futa High so I’ll visit every morning, okay? Okay? Okay?

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.730
Uh, okay…

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.000
I’m relieved.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.190
Over what?

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.110
You’re going after
the Ichijou sisters, right?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.850
No matter how you think about it,

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.470
the Ichijou sisters are a lot more fun to be with than the Sakurazuki sisters.

00:04:50.820 --> 00:04:55.830
Maybe it’s more natural for you or it’s easier to relax. Either way, it seems more pleasant.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.860
Is that so?

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.840
To reduce the economic inequities in Southeast Asia,

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:11.240
these initiatives are being adopted and realized.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.570
This is very likely to appear in a test, so be sure to remember it.

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:17.240
Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan are indeed childhood friends.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.250
Casual conversations with them are quite pleasant, but…

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.750
Are there any questions?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:25.670
Okay then, none?

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.970
Then we’ll continue on to the next section.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.910
But it’s fun to be with Kira-chan and Yura-chan too.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.140
Just like the previous chapter, this one involves economic and political reform.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.020
They are great girls after all.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.320
Nozomu-kun!

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.540
You’re doing good work on cleaning duty.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:49.780
Shall we help you?

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.790
Oh no, I’ll be fine.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.400
Come on, Yura-chan.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.330
Huh? You do it, Kira-chan.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.040
What’s the matter?

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:02.510
Umm, you see…
It’ll be Christmas soon, right?

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:03.360
Yeah.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.970
We want you to come to a party, Nozomu-kun.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:07.680
A party?

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.880
We’ll reserve a great restaurant.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.300
And forget about your entrance exams that day.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.660
And get lost in the excitement of the party.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.470
Oh yes, and we’ll have games there.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.360
A Christmas party, huh?

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:25.470
It was unbelievably fun when we were invited to the chateau during the summer.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.280
I’ll definitely go.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.060
That’s great.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.350
So here’s your invitation.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:33.910
It has the time and place listed.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.040
Okay, thanks.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.110
Okay, see you tomorrow.

00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:39.650
Yes, see you tomorrow.

00:06:39.650 --> 00:06:41.080
Bye bye!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.160
I’m really looking forward to the party.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.470
Partying with everyone in high spirits…

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.550
I hear that the Momoi-senseis will be coming this time.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.040
They’re preparing an adult cosplay.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.060
A-Adult cosplay?

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.940
So what will you get as a present?

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:09.630
Oh yeah, presents.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:13.490
Looks like everyone’s going to exchange presents valued under 500 yen.

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.080
Is that so?

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.050
Try to get it as cheaply as possible,

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:20.080
but make it look as expensive as possible –
I wonder how to do that?

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.920
Oh, I’m going to the bookstore.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.980
You’re getting a test question book or something?

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.640
Yes, for math.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:33.030
Sounds rough, aiming for a high-tier school.

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:35.730
I’m going home to play a game or something.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.490
Do your best, exam student.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:39.850
You’re one yourself, aren’t you?

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.120
Note: These books are math textbooks used in cram school.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:54.870
I have to concentrate more on math.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.580
Note: These books are astronomy books.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.580
I’ll buy a lot more of this stuff
after the exam.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.330
Until then, patience. Patience.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.920
Excuse me– oh, Yuuya!

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:11.800
Nozomu! It’s been a while, since summer.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.720
Yeah, I guess so.

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:19.290
I intend to confess to her when I get accepted into high school.

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.220
To Kaoruko-chan?

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.730
Yes. That’s okay, right?

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:24.770
Amazing!

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:38.030
I told you then, right?
That I’d confess to Kaoruko-chan.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.290
Uh, yeah.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.870
I’ve decided to do it on Christmas Eve.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:46.440
But you said you’d do it after you finished the exams.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:47.210
I am finished.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:51.300
I’ve been approved, on recommendation, to Hokunan University’s Annex.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.830
On the cover: “Space Flight Aerodynamics Studies”.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:59.180
You’re amazing, as expected. Congratulations.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.810
It’ll be okay if I confess, right?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:06.310
Why do you have to ask me for every little thing?

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:10.360
You’ve been acting weird ever since we went to the beach.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:14.780
You’ve been avoiding Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan like opposing poles of a magnet.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:22.070
We just had a little fight. We made up, and now we’re all friends again.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:27.080
Say, Nozomu. Perhaps you really do feel the same way about Kaoruko-chan?

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:31.410
What are you talking about? We’re nothing more than childhood friends!

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.950
Just childhood friends…

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.100
Is that so?

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:39.280
All right, I have to get back
to studying now.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:54.230
Nozomu-chan! What a coincidence.

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:56.610
Ah, yeah…

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:01.940
Great timing. I can show you the English reference book now.

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:04.370
No, I’ll be fine for today.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:08.630
Fine, you say? But you said this morning that it would help you.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:12.750
But that’s why… I’ll be fine for today.

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:16.750
Am I doing something unnecessary?

00:10:16.750 --> 00:10:20.760
Is lending a reference book considered unwanted help?

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.440
It’s nothing like that.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.300
But…

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:25.390
It’s nothing like that!

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.740
Yuuya’s in there…

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.120
He’s still inside, so…

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.120
Ah, is that so.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.410
If you go in there, Kaoruko-chan, I’m sure he’d be happy.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:50.870
Nozomu-chan, you’re acting really weird.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:54.090
I’m sorry! I have to take care of business!

00:10:54.530 --> 00:10:55.710
Nozomu-chan!

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:04.960
What the hell is your problem,
Nozomu-chan?

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.480
So what happened with Yuuya-kun?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.450
We must have just missed each other because we never met.

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:20.440
Oh well, that’s too bad.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:24.040
More importantly, Nozomu-chan’s attitude is terrible.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:27.250
He’s acting really weird.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:31.300
It’s like he doesn’t enjoy being around me.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.250
Maybe he’s in love with you…

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:38.020
Nozomu-chan is in love with you, Kaoruko-chan.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:39.500
Eh?!

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:40.940
Maybe that’s why
he’s so conscious about it.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:43.890
T-That’s impossible; it can’t possibly be.

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:46.020
You don’t think so?

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.310
Huh?

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:01.570
Ah, Sumireko…

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:06.830
Maybe you’re in love with him?
With Nozomu-chan?

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.790
It’s not…

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.780
So that’s how it is.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:17.800
But what about you, Kaoruko?

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.170
How do you feel about Nozomu-chan, Kaoruko?

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.330
I’m not really…

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:30.970
I see. you’re in love with Nozomu-chan… so that’s how it is, wow.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:32.670
Stop it! Stop it!

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:34.400
That’s so cute, Sumireko.

00:12:40.330 --> 00:12:42.430
Why haven’t you said anything until now?

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:45.720
I figured that you like him too,
Kaoruko-chan.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:49.880
And unlike you, I can’t say how I feel.

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:54.210
Don’t hold back – just tell him how you feel.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:55.920
Do you think so?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.660
I do!

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:59.090
Say, Kaoruko?

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:03.300
Please don’t tell anyone about this yet.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.070
Uh, okay.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:06.700
So will you confess to him?

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:09.280
No, it’s all right for now.

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:13.090
Being able to see him again and be close to him after all this time…

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:16.850
To enjoy a celebration with him and everyone else – that’s fine for now.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.310
Is that so…

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.360
Aw, it’s become so hot.

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:29.950
Oh, it’s Sirius.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:33.200
A young, first-magnitude star.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.460
No, I’ll be fine for today.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.140
Fine, you say…

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:51.680
Nozomu-chan!

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.430
I did it again.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.640
I sure am hopeless.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:01.150
I told you then, right?
That I’d confess to Kaoruko-chan.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:04.380
I’ve decided to do it on Christmas Eve.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:05.280
Huh?

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:08.870
I’ve been approved, on recommendation, to Hokunan University’s Annex.

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:11.540
I can’t win against him.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:14.650
Even though I have no chance against him,
it just pisses me off.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.880
I wonder how Kaoruko-chan feels about Yuuya.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:24.250
Say, Nozomu. Perhaps you really do feel the same way about Kaoruko-chan?

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:28.370
I don’t know, even though they’re my own feelings.

00:14:28.370 --> 00:14:31.400
Besides, I have Kira-chan and Yura-chan.

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.030
I’m deplorable, aren’t I?

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:47.780
Isn’t it great that Nozomu-kun accepted our invitation?

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:50.210
Yes, I’m looking forward to it.

00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:53.850
This is the first Christmas Eve we’re spending with Nozomu-kun.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:54.780
Yes.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.020
Man, I didn’t get enough sleep.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.120
What the hell are you doing, Nozomu?

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:16.700
Yeah, what the hell am I doing?

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:18.000
Are you okay, man?

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:21.100
Good morning, Nozomu-kun! Kosaka-kun!

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.570
Oh, good morning!

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:24.610
Good morning.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.920
Kira-chan, Yura-chan, you two are so cute even this early in the morning.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:41.370
Oh, Yuuya-kun! It’s been a long time.

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:46.030
On the 24th? Sure, as long as it’s before evening.

00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:50.380
Yes, yes, I guess so. So, see you later!

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:54.050
Perhaps it’s a date with Yuuya-kun?

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:59.630
Huh? Oh no, he just wants me to help him find a present for his little sister.

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:00.830
Is that so?

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:04.110
I’ll head straight to the party after that.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:04.900
Okay.

00:16:05.550 --> 00:16:07.670
And if he confesses to you suddenly…

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.820
Hey, don’t make fun of me!

00:16:12.190 --> 00:16:14.120
I’m sorry! I’m sorry!

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.190
Hey!

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.480
Onii-chan!

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:42.310
Lookey! Lookey!

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:43.480
Huh?

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:46.290
Ta-dah!

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:47.320
Wow, you’re very cute.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:51.790
So stay with Ruru and Rara at the party.

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:54.920
You can’t cheat on us with any of the other girls.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:59.870
Oh, Nozomu-kun, aren’t you going with everyone else?

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:03.550
I haven’t bought a present yet, so I’ll head out early.

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.670
So we’ll see you at the appointed meeting place, then.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:07.280
Yes.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.430
I wonder if Kaoruko-chan’s coming to the party.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:17.690
I guess I should apologize
to her about earlier.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:21.350
I’ve decided to do it on Christmas Eve.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:25.440
That has nothing to do with me.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:54.800
It’s snow! We’re going to have a White Christmas!

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:56.600
The weather report was right.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.600
Thanks for today.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:00.440
You’re welcome.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:03.150
It seems that I should be off.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:03.900
Okay.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.650
What’s the matter?

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:14.030
Can we meet again?

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:18.180
Yes. You’re my friend after all, Yuuya-kun.

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:20.740
Not as a friend.

00:18:22.220 --> 00:18:25.870
Since we were children, I was always watching you, Kaoruko-chan.

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:32.380
After a lot of thought I’ve come to the conclusion that I’m in love with you.

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:41.870
Well, I…

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:43.730
Is there someone else you’re in love with?

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:45.890
Uh, I’m not sure…

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.480
You don’t need to answer me right away.

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.960
It’s okay for now. It’s just fine being friends for now.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:04.330
From now on, I want you to notice me little by little.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:10.380
And if someday you have the same feelings as I do, then at that time…

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:12.330
I…

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:16.370
As friends, there’s no problem, is there?

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:17.840
Ah, no.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:19.920
That’s great.

00:19:20.710 --> 00:19:22.350
It looks like it’ll be harsh tonight.

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:23.990
It really does.

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:27.010
I’ll escort you.

00:19:27.010 --> 00:19:28.040
Thank you.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:37.610
Wow, I did check the weather report.

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:57.090
It has nothing to do with me, and yet…

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:59.870
It has nothing to do with me, and yet…

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:12.400
Nozomu-kun!

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:14.370
What the?

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:20.440
We’ve been waiting for you.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.990
It must have been cold.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:25.130
Where’s everyone else?

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:28.070
Where’s Keisuke? And the others?

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:30.330
Today is just for the three of us.

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:31.330
Huh?

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.580
It is our first Christmas Eve together.

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:50.780
Nozomu sure is late.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:54.020
He did say he was going to buy a present.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.810
I’m sorry I’m so late.

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:59.920
You didn’t see our Onii-chan?

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:01.400
He still hasn’t come yet.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.400
I wonder if he’s lost.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.160
You did tell him the address, didn’t you, Kosaka-kun?

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:10.420
Well, he knew about the party before I told him.

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:13.290
Speaking of which, Kira-chan and Yura-chan aren’t here yet either.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.050
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.050
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:16.020
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:16.020
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.900
Yay, it’s the New Year!

00:23:12.900 --> 00:23:15.120
Celebratory New Year’s dishes, New Year’s games, and New Year’s allowance!

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:17.280
And visiting the shrine on the first day of the year!

00:23:17.280 --> 00:23:20.960
Ruru and Rara will be helping out at the local shrine.

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:24.120
Next time – The Wandering Heart’s New Year’s Temple Visit
